# OpenRustClaw Project Rules

This is the OpenRustClaw project — a production-ready Rust AI agent framework.

## Quick Reference
- See `.cursor/rules/` for detailed conventions
- Architecture: Rust core (22 crates) + Python sidecar
- Gateway: Axum WebSocket server
- Agent: Runtime with tool execution

## New Module Rules

### Voice Module (`crates/voice`)
- Wake word detection uses Porcupine — always validate model path
- STT/TTS operations are async and may block — use `tokio::task::spawn_blocking`
- Audio streams must be properly closed on drop to prevent resource leaks
- Never store audio recordings without user consent
- Respect platform-specific audio permissions (mic/camera access)

### Canvas Module (`crates/canvas`)
- A2UI workspace uses WebSocket for real-time updates
- All canvas operations are collaborative — handle conflicts with OT/CRDT
- Session state must be cleaned up on client disconnect
- Validate all user-generated content before rendering
- Rate limit canvas operations to prevent abuse

### Mobile Module (`crates/mobile`)
- iOS/Android SDK uses gRPC for communication
- Device nodes (camera, location) require explicit permissions
- Push notifications must respect user preferences
- Mobile API endpoints require stronger auth (device attestation)
- Battery optimization: batch operations, minimize wake locks

## Inter-Agent Communication
- Agent-to-agent calls use `sessions_*` tool naming convention
- Always validate agent capability before routing
- Heartbeat scheduler maintains distributed agent state
- Router uses priority rules: capability match > load > latency
- Failed inter-agent calls should fallback to local execution

## Webhook Security Requirements
- All webhooks must verify signatures using HMAC-SHA256
- Reject requests from non-allowed IP ranges (CIDR validation)
- GitHub webhooks: verify `X-Hub-Signature-256` header
- Stripe webhooks: verify `Stripe-Signature` header
- Log all webhook events for audit trail
- Implement idempotency keys to prevent duplicate processing

## Multi-Agent Patterns
```rust
// Agent routing with capability check
let router = AgentRouter::new()
    .with_capability_check(true)
    .with_fallback(FallbackStrategy::Local);

// Inter-agent tool call
let result = router.call_agent(
    target_agent_id,
    ToolRequest::new("sessions_query", params)
).await?;
```

## Voice Patterns
```rust
// Wake word detection
let wake = WakeWordDetector::new(model_path)?
    .with_sensitivity(0.7);

// Continuous talk mode
let talk = TalkMode::new(stt, tts)
    .with_timeout(Duration::from_secs(30));
```

## Canvas Patterns
```rust
// Session management
let session = CanvasSession::new(session_id)
    .with_max_users(10)
    .with_collaboration(true);

// Operation broadcasting
session.broadcast(Operation::AddNode { ... }).await?;
```

## Channel Implementation
When adding new channels:
1. Implement `Channel` trait from `openrustclaw-core`
2. Add config section to `config/channels-example.toml`
3. Update `crates/channels/src/lib.rs` with feature flag
4. Include rate limiting and allowlist support
5. Add webhook verification if applicable

## Security Checklist
- [ ] All external inputs validated
- [ ] Secrets never logged or exposed in errors
- [ ] Rate limiting implemented for all public endpoints
- [ ] Webhook signatures verified
- [ ] File uploads scanned/sandboxed
- [ ] Auth tokens validated on every request
